            <ArticleTitle>The effects of nifedipine on coronary haemodynamics and exercise left ventricular function.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>35-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The effect of nifedipine on exercise left ventricular function and coronary haemodynamics was studied in a group of patients with coronary artery disease. Nifedipine, unlike nitroglycerin, appears to act as a primary coronary vasodilator and was able to reverse exercise induced changes in ventricular function.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
